From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:27:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sleep: keep SError masked until the way
 back is done

On 1.869 and 1.870 a J604 deep sleep reset the SoC 78 s after its
RTC alarm both times: the resume stub's 60 s WD2 window plus a cold
boot. The 80 s window set at the first line of apple_sleep_return()
was never reached. So the CPU stopped in the generic return:
cpu_resume, __cpu_suspend_exit() or cpu_suspend()'s
local_daif_restore().

That restore unmasks SError. One latched during the wake, by the wake
program, the boot object or a fabric that is not back yet, is taken
there, and with panic=0 the machine sits until WD2.

Mask DAIF before cpu_suspend() so that its restore leaves everything
masked, record ISR_EL1 after the way back, and unmask only at the end
of .enter, inside a WD2 window of its own (140 s), with
WDT_SUSPEND_SECS set again after it. The next reset then tells the
two apart: still 60 s means the generic return itself, 140 s means a
pending SError, and a later window or none means it got past both.
The wake log names a pending SError when one was seen.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
index 6d9bd3f5c5..a76580d461 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
@@ -75,6 +75,7 @@
 #include <asm/memory.h>
 #include <asm/smp_plat.h>
 #include <asm/suspend.h>
+#include <asm/daifflags.h>
 #include <asm/sysreg.h>
 #include <asm/virt.h>
 
@@ -155,6 +156,10 @@ struct aura_s2r_mailbox {
  */
 #define WDT_RETURN_SECS		80
 #define WDT_REWAKE_SECS		100
+/* Last on the way back: SError unmasked again, before device resume. */
+#define WDT_UNMASK_SECS		140
+/* ISR_EL1.A: an SError pending */
+#define SLEEP_ISR_A		BIT(8)
 
 #define AON_AP_DEADLINE		0x08
 
@@ -650,6 +655,8 @@ struct apple_sleep {
 	int radio_perst;
 	bool radio_perst_low;
 	bool returned;
+	/* ISR_EL1 just before SError was unmasked after a wake */
+	u64 isr_wake;
 	/* This wake came back down the deep path, not the DRAM-kept one. */
 	bool deep_ran;
 	/* This sleep's wake came from the SMC's sources alone. */
@@ -3334,6 +3341,7 @@ static void apple_sleep_return(struct apple_sleep *s)
 static int apple_sleep_enter(suspend_state_t state)
 {
 	struct apple_sleep *s = apple_sleep;
+	unsigned long daif;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = apple_sleep_refuse(s);
@@ -3373,6 +3381,11 @@ static int apple_sleep_enter(suspend_state_t state)
 
 	s->cntkctl = read_sysreg(cntkctl_el1);
 	pm_set_resume_via_firmware();
+	/*
+	 * Everything masked until the way back is done: cpu_suspend() restores what it
+	 * found, so an SError latched during the wake waits for our unmask below.
+	 */
+	daif = local_daif_save();
 	ret = cpu_suspend(0, s->soc->commit);
 	if (ret)
 		panic("Apple committed sleep returned without physical wake: %d", ret);
@@ -3384,6 +3397,11 @@ static int apple_sleep_enter(suspend_state_t state)
 	apple_sleep_stray_restore(s);
 	sleep_wake_restore(s);
 
+	s->isr_wake = read_sysreg(isr_el1);
+	apple_sleep_set_wd2(s, WDT_UNMASK_SECS);
+	local_daif_restore(daif);
+	apple_sleep_set_wd2(s, WDT_SUSPEND_SECS);
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -3682,6 +3700,9 @@ static void apple_sleep_report(void)
 
 	dev_info(s->dev, "back from sleep, boot object resumes %llu -> %llu\n",
 		 s->resumes_before, s->resumes_after);
+	if (s->isr_wake & SLEEP_ISR_A)
+		dev_warn(s->dev, "an SError was pending on the way back: ISR_EL1 %#llx\n",
+			 s->isr_wake);
 	for (i = 0; i < s->ps_unlatched_count; i++)
 		dev_warn(s->dev, "power word %#x was off with BUSY latched at the commit: %#x\n",
 			 s->ps_unlatched[i].offset, s->ps_unlatched[i].val);
-- 
2.43.0

